    "# AI & Machine Learning: Code, Train & Deploy\n",
    "## Week 13 — Deep Learning, Embeddings, and Audio Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syllabus focus:** deep learning; neural networks; TensorFlow/Keras; training deep learning models; hyperparameter tuning.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business context:** Popularity alone does not explain listener preference. Deep learning can help model hidden audio patterns and artist similarity that may be invisible in raw popularity metrics.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Capstone deliverable:** A similarity or embedding concept that connects artists with similar sound profiles.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Learning objectives\n",
    "- understand latent embeddings\n",
    "- compute similarity between vectors\n",
    "- connect embeddings to discovery and recommendation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "embeddings = {\n",
    "    'Nova Vela': np.array([0.92, 0.88, 0.74]),\n",
    "    'Luna Harbor': np.array([0.90, 0.85, 0.71]),\n",
    "    'Aster Vale': np.array([0.30, 0.42, 0.78]),\n",
    "    'Bright Echo': np.array([0.81, 0.83, 0.70])\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, vec in embeddings.items():\n",
    "    print(name, vec)\n",
    "\n",
    "base = embeddings['Nova Vela']\n",
    "for name, vec in embeddings.items():\n",
    "    if name != 'Nova Vela':\n",
    "        dist = np.linalg.norm(base - vec)\n",
    "        print(f'Nova Vela vs {name}: {dist:.3f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why this matters\n",
    "Embedding similarity helps discover artists who may not be highly popular but match a listener's taste based on latent audio structure. This is a major mechanism for long-tail discovery.\n"
  },
